you will let live !"]],"x":[[44007019,44007019,7],[20001016,20001016,4],[2001016,2001016,3],[19105025,19105025,3],[20004016,20004016,3],[66016004,66016006,3]],"xn":6}},"people":[{"id":"israel_682","name":"Israel","also":"","summary":"One who follows on another’s heels; supplanter, (Gen. 25:26; 27:36; Hos. 12:2-4), the second born of the twin sons of Isaac by Rebekah. He was born probably at Lahai-roi, when his father was fifty-nine and Abraham one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[1,5,7,9,12,13]},{"id":"judah_1751","name":"Judah","also":"","summary":"Praise, the fourth son of Jacob by Leah.","verses":245,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[2]},{"id":"reuben_2429","name":"Reuben","also":"","summary":"Behold a son!, the eldest son of Jacob and Leah (Gen. 29:32). His sinful conduct, referred to in Gen. 35:22, brought down upon him his dying father’s malediction (48:4).","verses":70,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[2]},{"id":"levi_1820","name":"Levi","also":"","summary":"The third son of Jacob by Leah. The origin of the name is found in Leah’s words (Gen. 29:34), “This time will my husband be joined [Heb. yillaveh] unto me.”","verses":64,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[2]},{"id":"simeon_2741","name":"Simeon","also":"","summary":"The second son of Jacob by Leah (Gen. 29:33). He was associated with Levi in the terrible act of vengeance against Hamor and the Shechemites (34:25, 26).","verses":40,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[2]},{"id":"benjamin_463","name":"Benjamin","also":"Ben-oni","summary":"The younger son of Jacob by Rachel (Gen. 35:18). His birth took place at Ephrath, on the road between Bethel and Bethlehem, at a short distance from the latter place.","verses":157,"father":"Israel","mother":"Rachel","v":[3]},{"id":"zebulun_3002","name":"Zebulun","also":"Zabulon","summary":"Dwelling, the sixth and youngest son of Jacob and Leah (Gen. 30:20). Little is known of his personal history.","verses":46,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[3]},{"id":"issachar_645","name":"Issachar","also":"","summary":"Hired (Gen. 30:18). “God hath given me,” said Leah, “my hire (Heb. sekhari)...and she called his name Issachar.” He was Jacob’s ninth son, and was born in Padan-aram (comp. 28:2).","verses":38,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[3]},{"id":"dan_973","name":"Dan","also":"","summary":"The fifth son of Jacob. His mother was Bilhah, Rachel’s maid (Gen. 30:6, “God hath judged me”, Heb. dananni).","verses":63,"father":"Israel","mother":"Bilhah","v":[4]},{"id":"gad_1262","name":"Gad","also":"","summary":"Jacob’s seventh son, by Zilpah, Leah’s handmaid, and the brother of Asher (Gen. 30:11-13; 46:16, 18).","verses":55,"father":"Israel","mother":"Zilpah","v":[4]},{"id":"naphtali_2149","name":"Naphtali","also":"Nephthalim","summary":"My wrestling, the fifth son of Jacob. His mother was Bilhah, Rachel’s handmaid (Gen. 30:8). When Jacob went down into Egypt, Naphtali had four sons (Gen. 46:24).","verses":49,"father":"Israel","mother":"Bilhah","v":[4]},{"id":"asher_337","name":"Asher","also":"Aser","summary":"Happy, Jacob’s eigth son; his mother was Zilpah, Leah’s handmaid (Gen. 30:13). Of the tribe founded by him nothing is recorded beyond its holding a place in the list of the tribes (35:26; 46:17; Ex. 1:4, etc.) It increased in numbers twenty-nine percent, during the thirty-eight years’ wanderings.","verses":43,"father":"Israel","mother":"Zilpah","v":[4]},{"id":"joseph_1710","name":"Joseph","also":"Zaphnath-paaneah","summary":"The elder of the two sons of Jacob by Rachel (Gen. 30:23, 24), who, on the occasion of his birth, said, “God hath taken away [Heb. ‘asaph] my reproach.”","verses":199,"father":"Israel","mother":"Rachel","v":[5,6,8]},{"id":"pharaoh_2330","name":"Pharaoh","also":"","summary":"The “new king who knew not Joseph” (Ex. 1:8-22) has been generally supposed to have been Aahmes I., or Amosis, as he is called by Josephus.","verses":5,"father":"","mother":"","v":[11,19,22]},{"id":"puah_2372","name":"Puah","also":"","summary":"One of the two midwives who feared God, and refused to kill the Hebrew male children at their birth (Ex. 1:15-21).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[15]},{"id":"shiphrah_2710","name":"Shiphrah","also":"","summary":"Beauty, one of the Egyptian midwives (Ex. 1:15).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[15]}],"places":[{"id":"egypt_362","name":"Egypt","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":26.4902,"lon":29.8808,"summary":"The land of the Nile and the pyramids, the oldest kingdom of which we have any record, holds a place of great significance in Scripture.","verses":564,"v":[1,5,8,15,17,18,19]},{"id":"pithom_953","name":"Pithom","kind":"City","lat":30.59385,"lon":32.18556,"summary":"Egyptian, Pa-Tum, “house of Tum,” the sun-god, one of the “treasure” cities built for Pharaoh Rameses II. by the Israelites (Ex. 1:11). It was probably the Patumos of the Greek historian Herodotus.","verses":1,"v":[11]},{"id":"raamses_965","name":"Raamses","kind":"","lat":30.59385,"lon":32.18556,"summary":"(Ex. 1:11).","verses":1,"v":[11]},{"id":"nile_895","name":"Nile","kind":"Water (River)","lat":19.21141,"lon":30.56733,"summary":"Dark; blue, not found in Scripture, but frequently referred to in the Old Testament under the name of Sihor, i.e., “the black stream” (Isa. 23:3; Jer. 2:18) or simply “the river” (Gen. 41:1; Ex. 1:22, etc.) and the “flood of Egypt” (Amos 8:8).","verses":30,"v":[22]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[428,8034,8034,8034,1121,1121,1121,3478,3478,935,935,4714,4714,854,3290,376,1004,1004,1004],[7205,8095,3878,3063,3063],[3485,2074,1144,1144],[1835,5321,5321,1410,836,836],[5315,5315,3290,3290,1961,7657,3605,3605,3130,3130,1961,1961,4714,4714,4714],[3130,3130,3605,3605,251,251,3605,3605,1931,1755,4191],[1121,1121,1121,6509,6509,8317,8317,8317,7235,7235,3966,3966,3966,6105,776,776,776,776,4390,4390,4390,4390],[2319,2319,2319,4428,834,3808,3808,3045,